00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.420
episode

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.420
"Winds of Arras,
\h              Answer Me..."

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.200
It's severe.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:27.970
It's too severe.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.770
Your punishment, I mean.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:34.110
The Queen was too heavy-handed by punishing you
with a month long disciplinary confinement.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:36.940
You've got it wrong, André.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.110
Wrong?

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:43.340
Win or lose, I expected to lose
my rank as Regiment Commander.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.990
Worst case scenario, I could have
been discharged from the military.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.520
By punishing me with a disciplinary confinement,

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.630
it would let the Duke save face and
allow time for things to cool down.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.690
I believe it was Lady Antoinette's act of kindness.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.130
I see...

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.340
I didn't realize the level of determination
you had for that duel.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.500
Don't look at me like that, André.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.720
Just think of it as some unexpected time off.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.380
I guess you're right.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.230
All right, if we hurry, we'll arrive in
the Village of Arras by late afternoon.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:15.350
For dinner, how about country-style
vegetable soup, bouillie de Calais,

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:18.650
and Arras Restaurant's handcrafted cheeses
and Calvados brandy made by its owner?

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.660
Sounds scrumptious!

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.150
Let's hurry and gallop there, Oscar.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.990
You're such a glutton.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:49.020
All right, it's only a short while longer
until we reach the Village of Arras.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.820
Oh, that's...

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.300
Sugane{Seguin}, right?

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.360
Long time no see.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.640
What's the matter?

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:10.840
It's me, Oscar.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.700
What business brings you here today?

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.110
Nothing, I just came to see how things were.

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:17.670
Is he your youngest? His name was...

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.740
Yes, his name is Gilbert.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.820
Hello, Gilbert.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.850
You were still a baby the last time I saw you.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:25.840
You've grown so big.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.080
Well then, please excuse us.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.640
Guess he didn't like me very much.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.240
I wouldn't say that.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.670
Still, I've never seen Sugane{Seguin}
act so unfriendly before.

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:02.460
Welcome!

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.190
Well, if it isn't Lady Oscar!

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.350
Long time no see.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:12.030
Well, well, look at what a
fine person you've become!

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:13.570
Great to see you too, André.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:15.560
It really has been a long time, hasn't it?

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.710
I heard you became the Regiment
Commander of the Royal Guards.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.270
I heard it through the grapevine.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.140
Your advancement is impressive!

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:24.740
I'm sure General Jarjayes is pleased, as well.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:27.420
Monsieur, could you make us
some of your specialty dishes?

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.820
We've been riding since this morning,
so we're starving.

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:31.220
Sure.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:35.090
I'll put all of my cooking skills into
action and make you a special dish!

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:36.410
Could I get another cup of tea, please?

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.290
Yes, coming!

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.810
Weren't you the one who read
the congratulatory speech,

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.180
for the School of Louis-le-Grand,
on the day of Louis XVI's coronation?

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.260
You remembered me. I'm...

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:59.110
...Maximilien de Robespierre.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:03.750
I'm Oscar François de Jarjayes,
Regiment Commander of the Royal Guards.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:05.690
I remember you, as well.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:09.570
I felt admiration for the beautiful officer
standing amongst the Royal Guards.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.960
Would you like to sit down?

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:12.530
Thank you.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:18.160
I'm currently studying law in
the advanced studies course.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:22.130
I plan to go to a university and
become a lawyer eventually.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:23.430
I see.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.630
Did you come to this village for a vacation?

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:29.070
A vacation?! Hardly!

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:32.140
I came to help the farmers in the next province.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:36.480
The unscrupulous monks at the monastery
are trying to take away their land.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:37.690
The monks are...?!

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.600
Yes, with their claim of God's
authority behind them,

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.230
they are preying on the weak!

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:49.940
De Jarjayes, I must say I terribly regret giving
that congratulatory speech on coronation day.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.900
Why is that?

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:57.770
We placed great hopes in the new King.

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:00.270
We believed a new era would come.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:01.120
Yet, look at us!

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.910
Our lives haven't changed one bit.

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:08.220
The price of goods rise by the day
and the people are exhausted.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.590
The whole country is dying!

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:15.280
They say the new Queen lives a
life of excessive self-indulgence.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.690
I also hear the Queen has the King
completely under her thumb.

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:24.500
The rising arrogance of the nobility and
clergy are causing the people to suffer.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.800
Don't you think all the blame lies with the Queen?

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.870
Please forgive me if I upset you.

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:42.180
What a fool I am.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:46.510
I forgot you're an officer of the Royal Guards, serving the royal family.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:49.880
Excuse me.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.220
This is for the tea, Monsieur.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:58.300
But please remember this.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.520
I will save this dying France!

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:06.940
It may be dying, but I love France.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.730
Well then, until we meet again.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:13.610
Oscar.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:16.160
Lady Oscar, don't let his words concern you.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:20.830
He means no offense. That man is just
too straightforward with his words.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.820
What sort of reputation does
Lady Antoinette have in this area?

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.530
Well...

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:30.500
Lady Oscar.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.710
What Robespierre said is true.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:40.240
Little by little, the people are beginning
to lose faith in the new King and Queen.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.940
Lady Antoinette!

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:48.230
Lady Antoinette!

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:53.020
Lady Antoinette!

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.330
Lady Antoinette!

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:00.130
I didn't realize you were here.

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:02.560
Everyone is waiting for you in the salon.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.530
I'm not interested in listening to a concert.

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:06.370
You mustn't say such things!

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:11.500
Watching plays, getting dresses made,
the balls... I'm sick of it all!

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.410
Come, please hurry.

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:14.900
Everyone is waiting.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.010
Come, come!

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:39.570
<i>She sings with such a gentleness to her voice!</i>

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.650
Say, who is that Lady?

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:56.550
She is Madame Polignac.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:57.600
Madame Polignac.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.990
<i>She's like the gentle shade of a tree.</i>

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:07.360
<i>It's as though she has the kindness of an angel.</i>

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:09.020
<i>I hope to be her friend...</i>

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.450
Boy, I'm stuffed!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:26.850
It was delicious!

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:32.350
Let's make the rounds tomorrow
and get some rest tonight.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:33.520
Yeah...

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:34.860
You seem down.

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:35.920
What's on your mind?

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:41.430
Don't worry about what Robespierre said.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.220
Lady Antoinette is the type of person
who is easily misunderstood.

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.400
It's nothing new.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:47.060
Still...

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.860
I see! That's terrible!

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.130
Something must have happened.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:53.230
Lady Oscar!

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.480
A child is deathly ill from a fever!

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.110
How?! Aren't there any doctors around?

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.410
There are no doctors in this village.

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:03.910
Even if there were, the cost to see
a doctor is too expensive, so...

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.460
Poor Sugane{Seguin}...

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:08.520
It's Sugane{Seguin}'s child?!

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.080
Could it be Gilbert?!

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.040
Hang in there, Gilbert!

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:38.190
Lord, please save him.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.010
Please protect my child.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:54.000
Well? How is Gilbert's condition?

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:59.920
You need to take him to a hospital immediately,
before it's too late, Sugane{Seguin}!

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:03.140
Father, we can sell the drawer and beds.

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:05.010
I'm fine with sleeping on the floor!

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:08.250
That won't be enough.

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:10.020
Darling, let's sell the cow.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:11.940
That's right! Let's sell the cow!

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:14.520
All right, we should hurry then.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.260
Let's rush him to the doctor in town.

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:17.400
Come on, Sugane{Seguin}!

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:23.560
No...

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:26.410
We can't... take him to the doctor!

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:27.620
Father!

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:28.910
Why?!

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:32.910
If we sell the cow, we won't
have anything to eat.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:36.140
All the field crops get taken away in taxes,

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:39.980
so our family manages to survive
by selling milk and cheese.

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:43.440
If we sell the cow... we'll starve to death...

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.890
The cow is worth more to you than your child?!

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:55.830
Don't be stupid!

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:57.100
You're his father, aren't you?!

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.610
I-In...

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.070
In what world...

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:07.070
...would a father not love his own son?!

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:11.240
I am the head of this household.

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:18.270
I can't make a decision that will subject us all
to starvation, in order to save one child.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.470
Poor Gilbert, but we have to give him up...

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.920
Your life is that harsh...?!

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:29.160
I don't understand...

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:32.030
We work so hard, yet why...

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:34.390
Yet, why are we only able
to eat salt and potatoes?!

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:37.540
Some blame the Queen...

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:40.350
But I... I just don't know...

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:01.500
F-Father...

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.250
Gilbert!

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:04.230
You need to be in bed!

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:07.630
Please don't be angry...
at my father... Lady Oscar...

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:11.640
W-We need that cow...

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:13.230
We'll be in trouble if we sell it...

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:18.440
Don't worry about me...
So please don't be angry at my father...

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:19.910
Gilbert!

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:28.620
André, get the horses!

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:30.320
Sugane{Seguin}, where is the hospital?!

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:37.490
<i>I had no idea...</i>

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:41.290
<i>To think that the people living on Jarjayes'
estate were this impoverished!</i>

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.450
I wonder if Gilbert will be all right?

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:07.930
Still, how is it possible that you
can't see a doctor when you're sick?!

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:09.200
What's happening to this world?!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.700
How is he, Doctor?

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.660
What is Gilbert's condition?

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:20.120
I cannot say anything for certain yet.

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:24.540
The rest will depend on his strength.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.050
However, his body is very weak.

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:29.170
We'll know either way by morning.

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:37.410
Gilbert...

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:52.870
<i>God...</i>

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:55.340
<i>Please save little Gilbert's life.</i>

00:16:55.340 --> 00:17:00.680
<i>Also, please subside the people's anger
towards Lady Antoinette as much as possible.</i>

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:04.480
<i>Please allow her kindness to be
understood by her people.</i>

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.020
Did you call for me, Your Majesty?

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:17.460
Please come closer, Madame Polignac.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:19.990
I would like to have a conversation with you.

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:23.560
I'm honored, Your Majesty.

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:29.840
I heard you came to Versailles six months ago.

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:32.400
So then, why is it that you have
hardly visited the palace until now?

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:34.820
That's because... Well...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.040
What is it?

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.550
That's because...

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:43.750
...we do not have enough money
to keep up appearances at court.

00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:47.710
Did I ask something I shouldn't have?

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:50.670
No, it's the truth, after all.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.270
<i>She doesn't have any money...</i>

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:56.140
<i>She's told me the most embarrassing thing
in the world with unclouded honesty.</i>

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:59.890
<i>She possesses such a pure heart.</i>

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:04.310
Madame Polignac, I would like us to be friends.

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:05.110
Please.

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:06.650
My, Your Majesty...

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.550
Move to the Palace of Versailles with your family,

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:13.450
so I may speak to you at any time.

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:14.660
The sooner the better, even tomorrow!

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:18.070
Your Majesty... The honor is more than I deserve.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.920
<i>Thus, after capturing Antoinette's heart,</i>

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:29.170
<i>Madame Polignac would soon control
Versailles for over a decade.</i>

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.040
<i>Furthermore,</i>

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:33.540
<i>she would unwittingly play a role,</i>

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:39.510
<i>that would eventually lead Antoinette
to her end as the tragic Queen.</i>

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:43.970
Lady Oscar.

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:08.070
M-Mom... M... Mom...

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:10.620
Mom...

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:12.740
Gilbert!

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:14.880
Gilbert!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:16.220
Thank goodness...

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:17.810
Thank goodness!

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:23.820
Thank goodness, Oscar.

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:25.310
Lady Oscar!

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:28.480
How is Gilbert's condition?

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:30.440
He's all right now.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.700
Thank goodness.

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:35.940
It's all thanks to you, Lady Oscar.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:38.150
If you weren't there...

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:42.740
It's very unlikely that he would
have been able to see a doctor.

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:48.050
Out of France's population of 20 million,
the nobles make up only 4 percent.

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:53.490
The lifestyle of the nobles and the court are
supported by the remaining 96 percent.

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:57.290
The majority of that 96 percent
are poor and starving,

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:59.630
unable to see a doctor when they are sick!

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:00.680
T-This is...

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:03.430
S-Sorry, I said too much...

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:16.740
You're exhausting the horses!

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:18.110
What's the matter, Oscar?!

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:23.140
I'm angry at myself for being so ignorant!

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:26.290
I didn't realize how truly poor the people were,
suffering from high taxes!

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:27.250
I know what you're saying!

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:30.890
But the King and Queen are kind-hearted people!

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:33.630
They're not the kind of people who would
willingly make their people suffer!

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:37.130
But the people's hearts are already
turning against the royal couple!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.550
Just who is to blame?!

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.060
Oscar! Are you all right?!

00:20:58.470 --> 00:20:59.490
<i>Oscar...</i>

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.960
<i>You're really something.</i>

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.590
<i>On the surface, you're as cold as ice,</i>

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:07.750
<i>but inside, your heart is burning like a raging fire!</i>

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:09.950
<i>And...</i>

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.950
<i>...that's why, I love you.</i>

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:25.080
<i>We placed great hopes in the new King.</i>

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:27.070
<i>We believed a new era would come.</i>

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:28.920
<i>Yet, look at us!</i>

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:31.350
<i>Our lives haven't changed at all.</i>

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.150
<i>I don't understand...</i>

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:37.590
<i>We work so hard, yet why are we only
able to eat salt and potatoes?!</i>

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:42.560
<i>Out of France's population of 20 million,
the nobles make up only 4 percent.</i>

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:47.780
<i>The majority of the 96 percent, who support
their lifestyle, are poor and starving!</i>

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:52.970
What was that just now?!

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:54.170
What's with you all of the sudden?

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:56.370
It's just the sound of the wind.

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:01.240
Right... the wind...

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:06.220
<i>Was it really the sound of the wind?</i>

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:11.160
<i>Or was it a giant, known as the people,
shackled by the chains of poverty,</i>

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:14.650
<i>letting out a sigh from the unbearable suffering?</i>

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:17.900
<i>The sound Oscar had heard,</i>

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:23.670
<i>may have been the faint heartbeat of the coming
revolution that would take France by storm.</i>

